---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'force-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Force converter — newtons, kgf, lbf | maratool',
  description: 'Convert newtons, kilograms-force, pounds-force, dynes, and poundals with exact NIST factors. Free browser force converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert newtons, kgf, and pounds-force',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert newtons, kilograms-force, pounds-force, dynes, and poundals with exact NIST factors. Free browser force converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert newtons, kgf, and pounds-force', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert newtons, kgf, and pounds-force"
      lead="Type a force value — read newtons, kgf, lbf, dynes, or poundals instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Datasheets mix newtons, kgf, and lbf constantly — especially for load cells, actuators, and fasteners. The <a href="/force-converter">Force Converter</a> converts between them with exact NIST SP 811 factors.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="force-converter" title="Try it — convert force units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Kilogram-force (kgf)" to "Newton (N)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Force conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the newton (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many newtons</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Newton (N)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kilonewton (kN)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kilogram-force (kgf)</td><td>9.80665</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gram-force (gf)</td><td>0.00980665</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pound-force (lbf)</td><td>4.448221615261</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ounce-force (ozf)</td><td>0.278013850954</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Poundal (pdl)</td><td>0.138254954376</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Dyne (dyn)</td><td>1.0000 × 10^-5</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>Quick anchors: 1 kgf = 9.80665 N exactly, 1 lbf = 4.448 N, and 100 N ≈ 22.5 lbf ≈ 10.2 kgf. When a spec says a button needs "3 N of actuation force", that is about 306 grams-force.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811" rel="noopener" target="_blank">NIST Special Publication 811</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/torque-converter">How to convert Nm to ft-lb for torque specs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/pressure-converter">How to convert PSI to bar, kPa, and atm</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/acceleration-converter">How to convert m/s² to g-force</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/force-converter">Force Converter</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
